      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Solve for $t$ if $4{t}^{3}-20{t}^{2}+24t=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $4t.$ We can factor out the $4t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{t}^{3}-20{t}^{2}+24t & =0 \\\\ 4t({t}^{2}-5t+6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression ${t}^{2}-5t+6$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4t({t}^{2}-5t+6) & =0 \\\\ 4t(t-2)(t-3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $t=0$, $t=2$ and $t=3.$",
